{{also|résilience}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|resiliō||to spring back}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹə.zɪl.ɪ.əns/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The mental ability to recover quickly from [[depression]], [[illness]] or [[misfortune]].
# The physical property of material that can resume its shape after being [[stretched]] or [[deformed]]; [[elasticity]].
# The positive capacity of an organizational system or company to adapt and return to equilibrium due to the consequences of a crisis or failure caused by any type of disruption, including: an [[outage]], natural disasters, man-made disasters, terrorism, or similar (particularly [[IT]] systems, [[archive]]s).

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|resile}}
* {{l|en|resilient}}
* {{l|en|result}}

